#### 5. Eager Test — `OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds` (line 52)

The test calls **7 distinct production methods** (`ValidateOrder`, `CalculateTotal`, `ApplyDiscount`, `ReserveInventory`, `ProcessPayment`, `SendConfirmation`, `UpdateOrderHistory`). A failure could stem from any of them.

```csharp
// ❌ Smell — 7 production calls, 1 assertion
processor.ValidateOrder(order);
processor.CalculateTotal(order);
processor.ApplyDiscount(order, "SAVE10");
processor.ReserveInventory(order);
processor.ProcessPayment(order, new CreditCard("4111111111111111"));
processor.SendConfirmation(order);
processor.UpdateOrderHistory(order);
Assert.AreEqual("Completed", order.Status);
```

**Fix** — test each step individually; if an integration workflow test is desired, mark it explicitly:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("Integration")]
public void OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds() { /* ... */ }
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Any failure requires debugging 7 methods to find the root cause.

