#### 7. Sensitive Equality — `GetOrderSummary_ReturnsFormattedString` (line 122)

The assertion compares against `summary.ToString()`, coupling the test to the exact format string.

```csharp
// ❌ Smell
Assert.AreEqual("Order ORD-001: 1 item(s), Total: $99.99", summary.ToString());
```

**Fix** — assert on structured properties instead:

```csharp
Assert.AreEqual("ORD-001", summary.OrderId);
Assert.AreEqual(1, summary.ItemCount);
Assert.AreEqual(99.99m, summary.Total);
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Any formatting change (currency symbol, whitespace, locale) breaks the test even when behavior is correct.

